## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design truly pluggable runtime behavior with correct isolation, hot-reload semantics, and safety in high-traffic environments.

## Key Concepts
- Runtime registries with atomic swaps
- Tenant-scoped policy resolution and default fallbacks
- Concurrency: lock-free reads vs. safe writes
- Validation of policy contracts and backward compatibility

## Code Example
```javascript
interface Policy {
  name: string
  apply(req: RequestContext, ctx: PolicyContext): Target | Promise<Target>
}
class Registry {
  private _store: Map<string, Policy> = new Map()
  get(name: string): Policy | undefined { return this._store.get(name) }
  swap(newStore: Map<string, Policy>) { this._store = newStore }
}
```

